Subject: [PATCH] fills: allow server-side marketId scoping

`getFills` / `getUserFills` / `countUserFills` scope by pool address, and
`limit` is applied to that pool-scoped result. On event contracts a binary pool
is recycled across successive markets, so one pool address carries the tape of
every market that has ever run on it — which `FillRow.market`'s own docs already
warn about ("Group and label by this, never by `pool` alone").

With no market field on `FillsOptions` there is no way to act on that warning
before the limit bites. Measured on testnet 2026-08-28, one 50-row page from
pool 0xc09e4a5bdee2899962727125fb5eaeb896798e46 spanned thirteen market
generations; at limit 5 on another recycled pool, a market returned 4 of its 5
fills with nothing in the response to say rows were dropped.

`market_id` is already selected by `FillQueryFields` and accepted by
`Fill_bool_exp`, so this is one optional field and one `where` clause. The
change is additive: existing calls are unaffected.

Reproduction: https://github.com/<AIRSPACE>/contributions/dreamdex/reproduce-fill-scoping.mjs
(no SDK install, no credentials — posts the same `where` shape to the same
public endpoint).

NOTE: `somnia-chain/somnia-markets` was not publicly readable at the time of
writing, so this diff is written against the shape of the published build
(`@somnia-chain/markets-sdk@0.28.1`, `dist/fills.js` / `dist/fills.d.ts`).
Line numbers will not apply cleanly; the change itself is three lines.

---
 packages/sdk/src/fills.ts | 21 ++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/sdk/src/fills.ts b/packages/sdk/src/fills.ts
--- a/packages/sdk/src/fills.ts
+++ b/packages/sdk/src/fills.ts
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-/** Options for {@link SomniaMarketsClient.getFills} / {@link SomniaMarketsClient.getUserFills}. All optional. */
+/** Options for {@link SomniaMarketsClient.getFills} / {@link SomniaMarketsClient.getUserFills}. All optional. */
 export type FillsOptions = {
   /** Max rows (default 50). */
   limit?: number;
@@ -8,6 +8,17 @@ export type FillsOptions = {
   since?: number;
   /** Only fills at/before this unix-seconds timestamp. */
   until?: number;
+  /**
+   *  Scope to one market's bytes32 marketId, applied SERVER-SIDE so `limit`
+   *  counts rows in THIS market.
+   *
+   *  Required for a correct per-market tape on binary: a pool is recycled
+   *  across successive markets, so `pool` alone selects every market that has
+   *  ever run on it and the limit truncates across generations. On SPOT/PERP
+   *  the pool address is the market id, so this is equivalent to `pool`.
+   *
+   *  See {@link FillRow.market}.
+   */
+  market?: string;
 };

 export async function getFills(
@@ -16,6 +27,7 @@ export async function getFills(
   indexerUrl: string,
 ): Promise<FillRow[]> {
   const where = applyFillWindow({ pool: { _eq: pool.toLowerCase() } }, opts);
+  if (opts.market != null) where.market_id = { _eq: opts.market };
   const data = await IndexerRead.gqlRequest(
     FillsQuery,
     { where, limit: opts.limit ?? 50, offset: opts.offset ?? 0 },
@@ -31,6 +43,7 @@ export async function getUserFills(
   const acct = account.toLowerCase();
   const where: Fill_Bool_Exp = { _or: participatedAs(acct) };
   if (opts.pool != null) where.pool = { _eq: opts.pool.toLowerCase() };
+  if (opts.market != null) where.market_id = { _eq: opts.market };
   applyFillWindow(where, opts);
   const data = await IndexerRead.gqlRequest(
     UserFillsQuery,
@@ -46,6 +59,7 @@ export async function countUserFills(
   const acct = account.toLowerCase();
   const where: Fill_Bool_Exp = { _or: participatedAs(acct) };
   if (opts.pool != null) where.pool = { _eq: opts.pool.toLowerCase() };
+  if (opts.market != null) where.market_id = { _eq: opts.market };
   applyFillWindow(where, opts);
   return IndexerRead.aggregateCount("Fill", "Fill_bool_exp", where, indexerUrl, headers);
 }
